/*  iterRefuseT -- A REFUSED ITERATE MUST REFUSE AND RETURN, NOT RUN AWAY.

    WHAT THIS PINS. When aCTionIterate is handed a source with no list it
    announces the refusal by name, poisons the cursor, and returns nothing.
    The enclosing advance then reads that poison and declines to move, so the
    while exits on the false it already trusts and the action carries on. The
    behaviour is one line of complaint and out.

    WHY IT NEEDED A ROW. Nothing in the fleet covered it, and the poison is
    the only thing standing between a refused iterate and an unbounded loop.
    The advance on a node that is not an iterator sets a count to one and then
    increments it forever, and every value it yields is true, so a while over
    it never ends. That is not a slow loop, it is a hang with no output to be
    suspicious of. Measured 2026-09-03 at over eleven million iterations in
    fifteen seconds.

    THE NEGATIVE CONTROL IS RECORDED, per rule H7. With the poison write
    removed from the refusal arm, row R hangs: exit 137 under a wall clock
    cap, seven and a half million lines of the line that must never print.
    With it present, row R refuses and the action returns. So this row fails
    when the mechanism is removed, which is the whole of what makes it a
    certification rather than a decoration.

    ROW R is the subject. It iterates a leaf that carries data and no list,
    then advances. The refusal line must appear, the walk line must not, and
    the statement after the loop must be reached.

    ROW W is the anti-vacuity sibling and it is not optional. Row R expects a
    walk of length zero, and a fixture whose iterate machinery was dead would
    also produce zero. Row W walks a real eight member group so that row R's
    silence means refusal rather than nothing happening.

    ⚠ ROW W NAMES ITS LAST MEMBER RATHER THAN COUNTING. A walk that stops
    early agrees with a walk that works if all either of them reports is that
    it ran, so the fleet asserts the presence of fifth, which only a walk that
    reached the end can print. The first draft of this row counted instead and
    was replaced for a measured reason: an undeclared counter incremented in
    an iterate body reads back zero while the walk itself is demonstrably
    complete. Both halves were seen in one run on 2026-09-03, the eight member
    lines printing and the counter reporting nothing. That is a separate
    finding and is reported rather than chased here; this row simply does not
    depend on it.

    READING IT. Both rows plus the sentinel must appear. A missing sentinel
    means the run truncated, and a missing row W means row R asserts nothing.
    A timeout means the poison is gone and the defect is back.  */
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking UnitTests Utilities list;
register(IterRefuse);
define
    irLeaf = 5;
    rowR argument code={
        print "R drive  iterating a leaf that has data and no list":;
        iterate g on irLeaf;
        while ++g;
            print "R BAD    the advance MOVED -- the cursor was not poisoned":;
        print "R ok     refused and returned; the advance did not run away":;
        };
    rowW argument code={
        print "W drive   walking a real eight member group":;
        iterate w on *argument;
        while ++w;
            print "W member" ~taG:;
        };
    ;
rowR(irLeaf);
rowW(sample);
print "ITERREFUSET SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
